2. GRANT OF RIGHTS (Internal Use)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Subject to Your compliance with the conditions in section 3 and the
restrictions in section 4, the copyright holders grant You a worldwide,
royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to:

  a. use, run, and execute the Work for Internal Use;
  b. modify, adapt, and create Derivative Works of the Work for
     Internal Use;
  c. distribute copies of the Work, and Derivative Works, to Your
     employees, contractors, and authorised agents solely to enable
     their Internal Use;
  d. study, test, evaluate, and audit the Work for Internal Use; and
  e. make, have made, and use the Work, and Derivative Works, in
     connection with Your own internal products, services, and
     workflows that are not External Commercial Use.

The grant in this section 2 is intended to permit use of the Work by
individuals, academic researchers, students, hobbyists, and commercial
companies for their own internal operations. It is not intended to
permit External Commercial Use.

