4. RESTRICTIONS
----------------------------------------------------------------------

You may not, without a separate written commercial licence from the
copyright holders:

  a. engage in any External Commercial Use of the Work or any
     Derivative Work;
  b. distribute the Work, or any Derivative Work, to any third party
     other than as expressly permitted under section 2(c);
  c. sublicense, sell, rent, lease, lend, or otherwise commercially
     transfer the Work or any Derivative Work to any third party;
  d. remove, alter, or obscure any proprietary notices or licence
     markings in the Work;
  e. use the trademarks, trade names, service marks, or product names
     of the copyright holders to endorse or promote any product or
     service derived from the Work without prior written permission; or
  f. claim authorship of, or right to, the Work or any Derivative
     Work.

For the avoidance of doubt, the foregoing restrictions apply to any
distribution of the Work in source or binary form, whether alone,
bundled, embedded, containerised, virtualised, or distributed via
network access.

